A||||4||Jake||what powers ignition coil?||||8||
Z||000000||Jake||07-04-2001||12:35 AM||||aright guys, I got a 85 ford f250 sittin in a parkin lot with no spark from the coil. I've already replaced the coil since I had one layin around but it didn't work. So I got to checkin it all out. I ain't gettin any power TO the coil at all. My question is, where does the coil get it's power. Tracing the power wire would involve tearing my wiring harness apart and I ain't up for that so I figured I'd see if you guys could help. this is one problem I've never ran into before. TIA||||reg||8
Z||000001||Terrybogin||07-04-2001||01:00 AM||||Time for a Duraspark box. Try smacking it with a blunt object, it may run long enough to get you home. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steve Normington||07-04-2001||01:23 AM||||One of two ways. Either the coil gets power directly from the ignition switch run/start position or from the ignition module in the distributor. I believe that most engines get the power from the ignition switch and the module grounds the coil. If this is the case, the coil should show 12 V to ground with the key in the run position.<p>[This message has been edited by Steve Normington (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Jake||07-04-2001||01:28 AM||||So what you're saying is, it's possible to just run a whole new power source to it by using a toggle switch or something? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Steve Normington||07-04-2001||02:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jake:<BR><B>So what you're saying is, it's possible to just run a whole new power source to it by using a toggle switch or something? </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>WARNING! Major weaseling.<BR>That I don't know, I've never worked on Fords. If the coil gets the power directly from the key and the module grounds the coil, then that might work. But, the module may also get power from the same circuit as the coil. You might see if your library has Mitchell books. There are a very useful source of step by step diagnostics and wiring diagrams.||||reg||1
